KG42.register("clusters-9c78ca6edb7e935e01d042d1",{"id":"35-microgrid_pool_strategy::v142-d-K004","paper":"35-microgrid_pool_strategy","label":"PCC exchange balance under the clearing interface and Case2 operating-mode constraints","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"PCC exchange balance under the clearing interface and Case2 operating-mode constraints","market_meaning":"The PCC exchange between the microgrid and the distribution system is constrained by the LLPM feasible region and capacity limits, and the intra-microgrid active- and reactive-power balance simultaneously constrains generation, load, and exchange quantities. Case2 additionally contracts the exchange range through a binary operating-mode quantity; this cluster expresses the exchange-feasibility obligation and does not yet constitute a complete islanding-duration rule or complete operational dispatch.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["activation","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The basic exchange balance and capacity interface are retained separately from the Case2 mode scaling. R004 only shares the basic clearing constraints, and R005 only shares the basic MG exchange-quantity interface; its robust objective does not become a dependency of this cluster, and it is not inferred that the robust approach and Case2 have been applied jointly.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"PCC exchange connects the DS clearing quantity and the intra-MG balance, forming an exchange condition that can be checked independently. It is retained separately from the DS welfare selection criterion because the Case2 mode constraints and intra-MG dispatch still have missing items. The shared capacity constraint is not counted separately as a new independent rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"This provides the clearing restriction on PCC exchange, the intra-MG balance, and the Case2 binary operating-mode scaling bound."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"This cites the basic LLPM capacity and clearing interface; the primary attribution remains in the clearing-pricing cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"This locates the MG exchange quantity in the DS welfare model and associates it with the MG-side PCC balance quantity; its robust objective is not introduced as an exchange obligation."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::E::v141-c-R008-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16"],"rationale":"The source states explicitly that PCC exchange belongs to the LLPM feasible set, and the capacity constraint plays different application roles for the same basic boundary in the clearing chain and the exchange-restriction chain; the Case2 scaling provision is retained separately."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-P-jt"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_pcc_active_jt","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-E15"],"rationale":"The same MG–DS active-power exchange quantity enters both the DS clearing objective and the intra-MG balance, constituting a cross-layer quantity interface; the source cost-sign narrative and power direction still need to be checked separately."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R008::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12"],"rationale":"Both places reference the same frozen clearing node, respectively as the subject of the clearing constraints and the source of the PCC exchange restriction, and R004 is selected as the display entry."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM02","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-E09"],"rationale":"Both places print the same basic capacity expression and participant scope; R008 emphasizes its use as a PCC restriction, so different functional bindings are retained. This duplicate association does not include the Case2 mode-scaling expression."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-P_it","v141-c-R008::x::x_participant_active_it"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-E09"],"rationale":"Both places are the generic active-power quantity within the same participant set of the baseline LLPM; the MG-subset use of R008 in Case2 is retained separately, and the generic array is not merged in its entirety with a particular MG quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-Q_it","v141-c-R008::x::x_participant_reactive_it"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-E09"],"rationale":"Both places are the generic reactive-power quantity for the same basic participant scope, retaining the different local uses in clearing and in the conditional exchange constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-P_min_it","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_pmin_it"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-E43"],"rationale":"Both places reference the same basic active-power lower bound; Case2 scales this bound through a binary quantity, and the scaling use does not change the independent preservation of the original parameter."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-P_max_it","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_pmax_it"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-E43"],"rationale":"Both places reference the same basic active-power upper bound, retaining the MG-subset and mode-scaling applicability conditions in R008."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-Q_min_it","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_qmin_it"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-E43"],"rationale":"Both places reference the same basic reactive-power lower bound, and the clearing-boundary use and the Case2 conditional use are maintained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-Q_max_it","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_qmax_it"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-E43"],"rationale":"Both places reference the same basic reactive-power upper bound; no capacity value is determined on this basis and no mode condition is removed."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-OM09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-P-jt","v141-c-R008::x::x_pcc_active_jt"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-E15"],"rationale":"The PCC active-power exchange of the same microgrid and the same time period plays different local roles in the DS objective and the MG balance, so it is associated and preserved separately; neither the original power direction nor the cost wording is rewritten."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R008-C003 freezes only the exchange-bound scaling of Case2 and does not freeze the total-duration control or the required duration definitions of source equation (56); therefore it does not yet express the complete T−τ islanding rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_islanding_rho_jt","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E43","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C is to supplement the manually checked equation (56), the total operating duration, and the islanding-duration definitions and indices; D does not add duration parameters or constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The Case2 bound mixes participant indices and microgrid indices, and the MG balance equation also retains the source notation in which a summation index and a universal quantifier appear side by side. The subset correspondence between generic participant power and the specific MG exchange quantity has not yet been explicitly frozen; zero exchange also cannot uniquely infer the islanding state.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_participant_active_it","v141-c-R008::x::x_participant_reactive_it","v141-c-R008::x::x_pcc_active_jt","v141-c-R008::x::x_pcc_reactive_jt","v141-c-R008::x::x_islanding_rho_jt","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-E29","v141-b-g02-E43","v141-b-g03-e003"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the indices, summation ranges, and mode meaning, and C is to clarify the MG-subset correspondence; the source notation is retained, and no identity relationship is fabricated from symbolic approximation or zero-exchange status."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The intra-MG generation capacity, start-up/shut-down and ramping limits, and dispatch objective have not been completely frozen with R008. The existing exchange balance and DS capacity interface are insufficient to prove that complete MG dispatch is feasible or optimal.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_gen_active_kt","v141-c-R008::x::x_gen_reactive_kt","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E05","v141-b-g06-E06"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If a complete operational execution rule is required, C should supplement the checked intra-MG dispatch objective and limits; the current candidate scope remains the exchange-feasibility conditions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"g01-E18 describes exchange cost with imports negative and exports positive, whereas the ULPM objective contains a negative price-times-exchange-quantity term; the bid branches also explicitly distinguish the direction of power exchange. The cost-sign narrative cannot directly serve as the definition of power direction, and the relevant original wording still needs to be checked.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-P-jt","v141-c-R008::x::x_pcc_active_jt","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E30","v141-b-g02-E32"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the notation and perspective of power direction, DS-side cost, and MG-side cost terms separately; at present only the same physical exchange quantity is associated, and the frozen cost-sign descriptions are neither unified nor rewritten."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence underlying the exchange balance, capacity interface, and Case2 conditions remains unverified, and the candidate same-quantity relationships and gap judgments have not undergone independent source review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E43","v141-b-g03-e003","v141-b-g03-e004"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the baseline and Case2 scope, power direction, indices, and missing duration conditions; in this round, no B audit, C2 independent review, or Agent E was performed."}]},"rule_refs":["35-microgrid_pool_strategy::v141-c-R008","35-microgrid_pool_strategy::v141-c-R004","35-microgrid_pool_strategy::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-aca52f9d7c02a0d7","COMP-b6b40cce13bbdd1d","KG40-e94214b4dec2eb9b"]});
